{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Like an eagle stirs up its nest.</b> A verb in active voice, and the meaning is that He leads them from place to place." "<b>And his young.</b> These are the small ones, and likewise ותור וגוזל. And the word גוזל is a general noun used as a term for chicks, like צפור." "<b>Hovering.</b> When they journey, from the root of מרחפת, and likewise the cloud over them when they journey." "<b>Spreads his wings, takes him.</b> He takes each and every chick until he bears it upon his pinion, for it has no strength to fly — and this is its meaning. Only, the interpretation of על כנפי נשרים connects with והבאתי אתכם אלי, and the meaning is that they went out with a high hand and came quickly to Mount Sinai, like the meaning of מי אלה כעב תעופינה."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "Resolved ג<b> as a stray markup letter prefixed to the lemma; the intended lemma is גוזליו from the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:53.880128764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}